    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d500">

                <pb facs="0808" n="798" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg798"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to Colonel Marshall S. Carter </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-06-29">29 June 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1015. My main point was to get the SCALS under Chinese flag and control at the
                    earliest practicable moment, Reurad 92890.<anchor n="70" xml:id="d500-f1"/> In
                    this connection your action has met my requirement. However, it is still
                    desirable to consummate the sale under the provisions of the Ship Sales Act as
                    soon as possible to avoid any possible repercussion coming about through United
                    States retention of title during this intervening period. Even the loan of a
                    United States ship though flying a Chinese flag is subject to challenge as
                    constituting support for one side against another.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d500-f1" n="70" xml:id="d500-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram of June 28, not printed.</p>
